## Bashan OS — privacy and proxy tools.
##
## All free software from Debian main. None needs an account, a sign-up, a
## credit card or a login. NO VPN service is bundled, no server list ships,
## and nothing here connects anywhere on its own.
##
## Measured marginal cost against the built image: 69.2 MB, 33 packages.

# --- Tor Browser ---------------------------------------------------------
# The LAUNCHER only, 60.0 MB. Tor Browser itself is NOT in the ISO: the
# launcher downloads it from the Tor Project on first run, verifies the
# developers' signature, and installs it into the user's home folder.
# That means Tor Browser needs an internet connection the first time, and
# that it updates itself afterwards without us shipping a browser we would
# then have to keep patched.
torbrowser-launcher

# --- the tor daemon ------------------------------------------------------
# 31.9 MB. Installed but DISABLED: hooks/chroot/0320-tor-disabled.hook.chroot
# turns the service off and fails the build if it is enabled, so it costs no
# idle RAM and opens no port unless the user deliberately starts it.
# Tor Browser does NOT need this - it carries its own tor.
tor

# 0.1 MB. Routes a chosen command through a proxy. Its shipped default
# points at 127.0.0.1:9050, which is where the tor daemon above would listen
# IF the user started it. Useless, and harmless, until then.
proxychains4

# --- VPN clients, no VPN service -----------------------------------------
# NetworkManager 1.52 speaks WireGuard natively - there is no plugin to
# install - and the kernel module ships with the stock Debian kernel
# (verified: wireguard.ko.xz in 6.12.111+deb13-amd64). wireguard-tools is
# what reads a .conf file.
wireguard-tools

# OpenVPN needs its NetworkManager plugin to appear in the Plasma network
# applet, so an .ovpn file can be imported with no terminal.
openvpn
network-manager-openvpn
